<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Bill type="bill" xmlns="http://leg.wa.gov/2012/document"><BillHeading><RequestNumber>H-3260.3</RequestNumber><ShortBillId>HB 2553</ShortBillId><LongBillId>HOUSE BILL 2553</LongBillId><Legislature>65th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2018 Regular Session</Session><Sponsors>Representatives Blake, Orcutt, Morris, and Hargrove</Sponsors><BillHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 01/10/18.</ReadDate><ReferredCommittee>Referred to Committee on Agriculture &amp; Natural Resources.</ReferredCommittee></BillHistory><BriefDescription>Adjusting assessments levied on hardwood processors.</BriefDescription></BillHeading>

<BillBody>
<BillTitle>AN ACT Relating to adjusting assessments levied on hardwood processors; amending RCW 15.74.060; and providing an effective date.</BillTitle>
<EnactedClause />
<BillSection type="amendatory" action="amend">
<BillSectionHeader><BillSectionNumber><TextRun>Sec. </TextRun><Value>1</Value><TextRun>.  </TextRun></BillSectionNumber><SectionCite><TextRun>RCW </TextRun><TitleNumber>15</TitleNumber><TextRun>.</TextRun><ChapterNumber>74</ChapterNumber><TextRun>.</TextRun><SectionNumber>060</SectionNumber></SectionCite> and 1991 c 67 s 3 are each amended to read as follows:<Caption>Assessments<TextRun fontFamily="Times New Roman">—</TextRun>Generally.</Caption></BillSectionHeader>
<P>To provide for permanent funding of the Washington hardwoods commission, agricultural commodity assessments shall be levied by the commission on processors of hardwoods.</P>
<P postPadding="halfline">An assessment is hereby levied on hardwood processors operating within the state of Washington. The assessment <TextRun amendingStyle="strike">categories</TextRun> shall be based on the hardwood processor's production per calendar quarter. The assessment shall be <TextRun amendingStyle="strikemarkleft">levied based upon the following schedule:</TextRun></P>
